<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of the Algarve</h1><p class="st-meta">1249 CE – 1910 CE · capital Faro</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Portugal's southern coast, held as a nominally separate kingdom by the Portuguese crown from its conquest until 1910.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-iii-of-portugal">Afonso III of Portugal</a> completed the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a> by taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faro">Faro</a> in 1249. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> disputed the territory until the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a> of 1267, after which Portuguese kings styled themselves Kings of Portugal and the Algarve.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a> had no separate institutions: it was governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> as part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a>, though its title and arms were kept as a mark of conquest. Its ports, especially <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-lagos">Lagos</a>, served as bases for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry the Navigator</a>'s voyages to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. Fishing, salt, figs and almonds sustained its economy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The title was later expanded under Afonso V, from 1471, to cover territories in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. The Kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a> ended in law with the Portuguese monarchy in the revolution of 1910 and became a region of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-portuguese-republic">First Portuguese Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-the-algarve.jpg" alt="Kingdom of the Algarve" width="320" height="235"><figcaption>Image: Grandprez, Carlos de (16..-17..?). Graveur · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reyno_do_Algarve_-_btv1b53227056j_(1_of_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1249 CE – 1910 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Faro</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Afonso III, Denis</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Portuguese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Reino do Algarve</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1580&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-algarve" aria-label="Kingdom of the Algarve on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4469 839 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of the Algarve lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4789 1095L4794 1282M4789 1095L4773 1045"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4794 1282h0M4773 1045h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4789 1095h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4789 1095h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1580&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-algarve">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
